# Codex Instructions

## Code Quality Rules

- No emoji characters in source code
- No inline imports in Python
- No unnecessary one-liner docstrings or narrative comments
- Comments only for non-obvious WHY
- Auto-format with available tools (ruff, prettier, gofmt, shfmt)

## Behavior

- Investigate before acting
- Fact-check claims independently
- No shortcuts or low-hanging-fruit reaching
- One specific recommendation, not a menu of options
- Push back when something feels wrong

## Constraints

- Always use `uv` for Python environments
- Never deploy to production without explicit instruction
- Never use `gh` CLI
- Write natural prose (no staccato, no em dashes)

